<BaseLayout title="Database & Ranking Methodology" description="How OpenAgent.bot classifies projects, attributes facts, assesses lifecycle and publishes open AI and robotics rankings." path="/methodology">
  <div class="page-shell"><div class="page-grid">
    <section class="page-section"><span class="kicker">Methodology / v0.1</span><h1 class="page-title">How the database works</h1><p class="lede">Classification, evidence, lifecycle states and ranking publication rules.</p></section>
    <section class="page-section methodology-layout">
      <nav aria-label="Methodology sections"><span class="data-label">On this page</span><a href="#categories">Categories</a><a href="#inclusion">Inclusion</a><a href="#lifecycle">Lifecycle</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a><a href="#rankings">Rankings</a><a href="#coverage">Coverage</a><a href="#corrections">Corrections</a></nav>
      <article class="prose">
        <h2 id="categories">Four primary databases</h2><p>Every public project has one primary category: foundation model, agent, robot model or robot hardware. Supporting infrastructure—datasets, simulators, SDKs, protocols and tools—remains searchable but does not compete in a primary homepage ranking.</p><p>Robot models are further separated into learned intelligence, world or physics models, and versioned simulation or mechanical assets. A physical robot never competes with a policy model.</p>
        <h2 id="inclusion">Inclusion and openness</h2><p>A project needs a stable upstream identity and at least one official or canonical source. Code, weights, hardware design or another material implementation facet must be publicly inspectable. Code, weights, data, hardware, documentation and governance openness are tracked separately; “open” is not one inferred boolean.</p>
        <h2 id="lifecycle">Lifecycle is an assessment</h2><p><strong>Active</strong> projects have a recent qualifying update. <strong>Cooling</strong> projects have slowed relative to their category window. <strong>Dormant</strong> means no qualifying activity inside the longer dormant window, not that a project is definitively dead. <strong>Archived</strong> requires an official archive, discontinuation, deprecation or supersession signal.</p><p>Initial cooling windows are 90 days for agents, 180 days for foundation and robot models, and 365 days for robot hardware. Dormant windows are respectively 365, 540 and 730 days.</p>
        <h2 id="sources">Source priority and time</h2><ol><li><strong>Canonical:</strong> repository APIs, package registries, model repositories and release metadata.</li><li><strong>Official:</strong> organization documentation, product pages, newsrooms and research pages.</li><li><strong>Community:</strong> attributable third-party evaluations and maintainer evidence.</li><li><strong>Discovery:</strong> signals that suggest a source to review, but cannot establish a material fact alone.</li></ol><p>Every material value carries a source, observation time and confidence. Collection failure retains the last known value with staleness; it never silently writes zero.</p>
        <h2 id="rankings">Ranking families</h2><p><strong>Activity</strong> tracks sustained maintenance. <strong>Momentum</strong> tracks change over a historical window. <strong>Adoption</strong> reports source-specific following or usage. <strong>Evaluation</strong> orders only comparable benchmark results with attributable version, task, hardware and evaluator conditions.</p><p>The current update ranking orders the freshest qualifying release, commit, official verification or product record and uses category-specific lifecycle windows. Stars appear only in the adoption view.</p><p>Historical Momentum requires at least 30 comparable history days, 80% required-metric coverage and 10 eligible projects. Until all three pass, the site displays “Collecting” rather than publishing a movement score.</p>
        <h2 id="coverage">Coverage is part of the result</h2><p>“Complete” means the database shows which required fields are present, fresh and attributable. Unknown fields remain unknown. A ranking or evaluation with insufficient coverage is withheld even when enough projects exist.</p>
        <h2 id="corrections">Corrections preserve history</h2><p>A correction creates a new observation and keeps the earlier record. Source conflicts are preserved until a field-specific selection rule or reviewed correction resolves them. <a href="/corrections">Submit a correction →</a></p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
